##MPC_score=(from dbNSFP5.2c_grch38) A deleteriousness prediction score for missense variants based on regional missense constraint. The range of MPC score is 0 to 5. The larger the score, the more likely the variant is pathogenic. Details see doi: http://dx.doi.org/10.1101/148353. Multiple entries are separated by ";", corresponding to Ensembl_transcriptid.
##fathmm-XF_coding_score=(from dbNSFP5.2c_grch38) fathmm-XF p-values. Scores range from 0 to 1. SNVs with scores >0.5 are predicted to be deleterious, and those <0.5 are predicted to be neutral or benign. Scores close to 0 or 1 are with the highest-confidence. Coding scores are trained using 10 groups of features. More details of the score can be found in doi: 10.1093/bioinformatics/btx536.
